<title>USA: Qualcomm says judge denied Motorola motion.</title>
<headline>Qualcomm says judge denied Motorola motion.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qualcomm Inc on Thursday said a judge in California denied Motorola Inc's motion aimed at preventing Qualcomm from selling its Q phone.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the company said the judge ruled Qualcomm's phone was not the same as equipment made by Motorola.  </p>
<p>The U.S. federal court judge previously issued a temporary restraining order against Qualcomm preventing the company from manufacturing, selling or distributing the wireless Q phone.</p>
<p>Motorola alleged that Qualcomm copied the design of its handheld Star TAC digital cellular phone.</p>
</text>
